#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fake-qemu - stand-in for qemu-system-x86_64 used by tests/run-tests.sh.

It parses the subset of the qemu command line used by the host scripts, serves a
minimal QMP, and simulates the guest by inspecting the attached ISOs:

  * WTL_JOB ISO (JOB.JSON + PAYLOAD.ZIP)  -> simulates guest/agent.ps1:
      AGENT_START, JOB_WAIT, JOB_FOUND, COPIED, EXTRACTED, LAUNCHED, READY/PROC_EXIT
    and runs a python version of the demo line protocol on each hostfwd host port.
    A "fake-behavior.json" in the zip changes the program behaviour:
      {"mode":"crash","code":3}  PROC_EXIT before READY
      {"mode":"hang"}            never listens (READY never comes)
      {"mode":"wrong"}           listens, but answers the protocol wrongly
      {"mode":"normal","delay":S} listen after S extra seconds
  * WTL_BUILD ISO (autounattend.xml)      -> simulates the unattended build:
      checks the XML parses and has no @PLACEHOLDER@ left, writes to the disk image,
      emits WU_ROUND lines (unless build.json updates=false), BUILD_DONE, exits 0.
  * anything else                         -> silent; runs until killed / quit.

Environment:
  FAKE_QEMU_SPEED         delay multiplier (default 1 = each step ~0.1-0.5 s; 0 = instant;
                          10 = ten times slower)
  FAKE_QEMU_LOG           append one JSON line per invocation {"pid","cwd","argv"}
  FAKE_QEMU_PIDDIR        write an empty file <pid> there while alive (leak tracking)
  FAKE_QEMU_MAX_LIFETIME  hard self-exit after N seconds (default 3600)
  FAKE_QEMU_BUILD_FAIL    if set, the build simulation emits BUILD_FAIL with that text
Stdlib only, python 3.8+.
"""
